mod_datalynx changes
====================

2026-11-17
----------

- Fix (#314): saving an entry again without changing a field no longer reports
  that field as changed for text areas, editors, files, tags, URLs and YouTube
  links, so rules that run only when a field changes do not run again. One
  comparison decides "unchanged" for every field type, comparing values as
  they are stored. Saving a YouTube link no longer raises a PHP warning, and
  youtu.be, embed and shorts links are understood.
- Fix: the cleanup of empty content rows (#308) kept only the content column
  in view; a course group field with a fixed course keeps the group in
  content1, so its rows were dropped on saving and by the upgrade.
- Fix (#315): a value "0" is no longer lost or mistaken for empty: text and
  text areas store and show "0"; a single choice left on "Choose..." stores no
  value (it was stored as 0, which "is empty" filters missed; upgrade
  2026111700 removes those rows); a required duration of 0 is refused; options
  labelled "0" can be added, and saving the options keeps choices of labels
  that are numerically equal ("5" and "05"); the quick search and the custom
  filter search for "0"; grouping keeps a group "0" and tells "01" from "1";
  rating aggregates of 0 are shown; the datalynx view field keeps numeric
  values of its options.
- Fix (#316): number and duration fields are searched as numbers (before, the
  stored text compared "10" < "9", so "> 5" found neither 10 nor 3), also with
  a decimal comma and for NOT; number fields sort as numbers. A numeric text
  field keeps decimals, and the unique check of text fields compares whole
  values ("a_c" is no duplicate of "abc").
- Fix (#317): ids are compared as whole numbers. A notification rule for team
  field 12 no longer runs when team field 2 (or 1) changes; the quick search for
  an option label of a multiple choice field no longer finds entries with
  option 21 when it means option 2; adding several entries at once
  (##addnewentries##) is checked as adding, not editing, and opening that form
  no longer shows an error; renaming a field or layout from "10" to "010"
  updates the views; a sorted filter keeps its sort by internal fields (time
  created, ...) when read back from its URL; the tag index lets authors see
  their own tagged entries.
- Fix (#318): editing a saved filter or a behavior condition shows the saved
  values of number, time, team member and tag criteria (they arrived as JSON
  text and were read character by character); saving it again no longer loses
  them.
- Fix (#319): an edit that resets the approval (approval on update) now counts
  as a change of the approval for rules, and an approval value a user may not
  set does not; a team member select that was not submitted no longer reports
  all members as removed; a full team no longer offers "subscribe"; rules
  triggered by the cron no longer act on the entry whose id equals the
  instance id; CSV import matches single choice labels as text; the course
  group menu without a course is no longer off by one; restore stores mapped
  field and user ids as numbers.

2026-11-16
----------

- Fix (#304): views whose saved filter selects approved or not approved
  entries load again in the browse web services. A saved criterion the strict
  criteria check refuses (a deleted field, an unselected row of the old filter
  form) is now left out of the view's request with a debugging message instead
  of failing the whole view.
- Fix (#305): filters on the institution or department of team members work
  again. Since April 2026 the team member profile fields were missing from the
  instance, so such a criterion was ignored and the filter returned all entries
  (for example "station leaders see their department" showed every
  department); since the strict criteria check the view failed instead. Sites
  that limit what a role sees with these filters should check what was visible
  in the meantime.
- Fix: the quick search finds entries by the labels of their single choice
  options and by the names of their team members again (broken since April
  2026), also for members no longer enrolled and whatever form the member list
  is stored in.
- Fix (#306): a PDF view whose stored settings cannot be read no longer fails
  the whole activity page. Settings whose string lengths a charset conversion
  broke are repaired; unreadable ones fall back to the defaults with a
  debugging message. Stored settings no longer instantiate classes other than
  stdClass.
- Fieldgroups: the list of subfields is stored in one form, "fieldid" or
  "fieldid:format|behavior|layout". The upgrade and restore convert older lists
  (bare numbers, empty slots that showed as "#NaN" rows in the subfield
  settings). Restore now also maps a subfield created after its fieldgroup;
  before, its id was lost. Deleting a field used in a fieldgroup with a
  behavior or layout is blocked like any other subfield, and such subfields are
  expanded correctly in views.
- Fix (#307): saving an entry no longer stores the empty lines of a fieldgroup
  with a file, picture or masked date subfield. Whether a line holds a value is
  decided by its subfields' own empty check, for saving and for validation.
- Fix (#310): when the entry form fails validation, the page no longer repeats
  every message without a field name above the form. Messages are shown at
  their fields; only one that no field shows appears on the page, named by its
  field.
- Fix (#308): a field left empty stores no content row; a missing row means no
  value. Before, saving stored the element's empty export ('0' for a date or a
  duration, '' or '[]'), so "is empty" filters missed those entries and "NOT
  empty" found some of them. The "is empty" search now also treats these
  stored placeholders as empty, and the upgrade and restore remove them, except
  in fieldgroup lines, whose rows keep the lines in place. File and picture
  fields keep their rows. Required lines of fieldgroups are checked as before.
- Fix: updating an entry that the view had not loaded (web services, imports)
  added a second content row for every field instead of changing the stored
  one.
- Fix: the "NOT empty" search on a team member or single choice field with no
  stored values failed on PostgreSQL.
- Team member select (#309): members the field no longer offers (e.g. no
  longer enrolled) cannot be kept by the edit form. Saving the entry for any
  reason removed them silently; the edit form now warns at the field that they
  will be removed, and saving names who was removed.
- Fix (#305, continued): filters on the institution or department of team
  members found nothing, because they looked for the member ids in a stored
  form that is no longer written. They now read the member lists. "My
  department" with an empty own department matches nothing (before it would
  have matched almost every team); deleted users are not members; NOT selects
  the entries without such a member.
- Saved filters keep their criteria in one form; saving, the upgrade and restore
  write it: "I am a team member" stores no user (it always means the current
  user; the filter settings showed whoever saved the filter as selected), user
  ids as numbers, no criteria or sort entries on fields that no longer exist
  (they made the view fail in the browse services). Restore maps the users in
  team member criteria. Team member lists are normalised once more. Leftover
  search and sort user preferences, which nothing reads, are removed.
- A team member select field whose institution or department a filter searches
  cannot be deleted, like any other field a filter uses.
- Team member select in fieldgroups (#312): inside a fieldgroup the field is a
  plain list of people, one per line. The team features that act on the entry
  as a whole no longer apply there: edit rights and visibility for team members
  (before: only the members of the first line got them), self subscription
  (before: always wrote to the first line; the link is gone and the web service
  refuses), the team field and member notifications. Members of the first line
  who had edit rights through such a field lose them. The settings forms of the
  team member field and of the fieldgroup say so.
- Fix (#313): restore never knew the datalynx version of a backup. Every
  restore, import and duplication reset the entry wrapper of grid views to
  "entry", and the migrations for old backups (field formats, view link tags)
  never ran. Backups now carry the plugin version. Backups without it (made
  before this fix) keep a grid wrapper they name and get the migrations, which
  change only what is old. The tag migration of restored instances failed on a
  wrong column; it now runs during the restore instead of as an ad-hoc task.

2026-11-15
----------

- Entries (#266): the entry form and a new web service, mod_datalynx_submit_entry
  (also in the Moodle App service), save entries through one submission service
  with the same rules: only fields the view lets the user edit are taken, every
  value is cleaned by its field's input contract, required is decided by the
  behaviors alone (availability conditions included, and also for a field left
  out of the submission), and each field validates its value. Fieldgroup lines
  are now validated on the server; before, their validation never ran.
- Behavior change: required select, radio, file, location and editor fields are
  checked on the server, not only by the form's own rules; the editor check
  never worked. A number that is given must be numeric even if not required.
- Removed: the ##*status## tag (the upgrade turns it into ##status##) and the
  schedule field's own "required"; required is a behavior setting only. The
  course group field now follows behaviors like every field.
- Fix: the inline profile editor wrote the author's profile while validating,
  also when the submission then failed. It now writes after saving.
- Fix: a multiple choice field no longer takes values that are not its options
  unless the tag allows adding options; the count of a user's entries includes
  entries added in the same request.

- Security: the view browse web services (grid, tabular, CSV, PDF, report) take
  search and sort criteria only as JSON that passes the strict criteria check
  the Moodle App service uses: fields of this instance, operators those fields
  take, scalar values. Anything else, including PHP-serialized strings, is now
  refused with an invalid parameter error instead of being passed to the filter
  or silently ignored. A view that forces its filter ignores a client's filter
  id, search and criteria in these services, as the app service already did.
- Fix (#303): the custom filter choice "missing" on a file or picture field
  found the entries that have a file. File and picture fields are now searched
  like every other field: the operator "empty" finds the entries without a
  file, NOT empty those with one. View filters and rule conditions show the
  usual is/not control for them; custom filters keep the exists/missing choice.
  The upgrade rewrites stored file criteria so that every saved filter and rule
  keeps finding what it found before.
- Fix: custom filters no longer put their "any of / all of" toggle among the
  selected options of multiple-choice fields.
- Fix: field values of "0" are shown in the AJAX grid, tabular and CSV views
  instead of being dropped as empty.
- Code: the browse steps of all view managers and the Moodle App payload live in
  one base class, `view\manager\view_manager`, and the web services share their
  parameters and filter handling in `external\browse_request`. Tabular, CSV and
  PDF views now also load the content of fields inside a fieldgroup, as grid
  views did. `get_browse_payload()` takes a datalynx instance or its id.
  Fields can accept search operators beyond those their search forms offer
  (`datalynxfield_base::get_accepted_search_operators()`).

2026-11-04
----------

- Moodle App: grid and tabular views can be browsed in the app, with view and
  filter switching, search and a growing list. Other view types offer a link to
  the web. Entries are read-only in the app for now, and this has not been tested
  on a device yet. The mock page shown in the app so far is gone.
- Security: acting on an entry from a view (`view\base::confirm_view_action()`)
  now requires that view to belong to the same datalynx instance and to be visible
  to the user. Before, a view of another instance holding the action tag could
  authorise the action, and visibility was checked on the current view instead of
  the requested one. Entry ids given to `process_entries()` are bound as query
  parameters, and only whole numbers count as ids.

2026-10-22
----------

- Code: datalynx-owned methods now declare native return types. Base-class
  methods that subplugins override carry them too, among them
  `datalynxfield_base` (`update_content`, `format_content`, `get_sort_sql`,
  `get_supported_search_operators`, `is_internal`, ...), `datalynxfield_renderer`
  (`replacements`, `render_edit_mode`, `render_search_mode`, `validate`,
  `patterns`), `field_format\base::config_form`, the field, view and field
  format settings forms (`field_definition`, `format_definition`, ...),
  `view\base` and `datalynxview_patterns`, and `rule\base::trigger`.
  **Third-party datalynxfield_, datalynxview_ and datalynxrule_ subplugins that
  override these methods must declare the same or a narrower return type**,
  otherwise PHP stops with a fatal "Declaration must be compatible" error. All
  subplugins shipped with datalynx are updated. Overrides of core methods
  (forms, events, tasks, privacy, backup) stay untyped, like core.

2026-08-11
----------

- Fields: added the **Schedule** field type. One field holds either a single date
  and time or a weekly pattern - weekdays, a time of day and the period it runs -
  and knows which of the two it is. Because a one-off carries the weekday of its
  own date, one query serves both: searching for a date finds the ride booked that
  day *and* every commute that runs on that weekday, and a rule can match a one-off
  request against a recurring offer. Searching and matching are day-granular by
  default; a narrower tolerance is a per-field setting.
- Itinerary: stops no longer carry a planned time, and the field no longer offers
  "require a time for every stop". A route says where a journey goes, not when: a
  date on a stop could not describe a ride that runs every Monday, and a ride
  entered without one was invisible to the time check and so matched every route it
  overlapped. Use a Schedule field beside the route instead. The unread
  `timeplanned` column is dropped from the derived waypoint index.
- Rules: the itinerary "within tolerance" relation is gone with it; the same
  relation on a Schedule field replaces it, and as an ordinary search criterion
  rather than a post-filter, so it narrows before the match limit applies.
- Ridesharing: `cli/migrate_ridesharing_schedule.php` converts an existing board -
  its pattern radio button, weekday multi-select, time select and the dates on its
  routes - onto one Schedule field, and rewires the views, the matching rules and
  the search form. It reports every entry whose old fields contradicted each other
  rather than guessing silently.

2026-08-10
----------

- Rules: the **Event notification** rule can now look for other entries that match
  the one an event touched, and notify the people behind both. Each row of the new
  **Matching entries** block compares one field against the value the triggering
  entry holds for it: the same value, a different value, within a tolerance of it
  (time, number and duration fields, and an itinerary's departure), or a route that
  can carry it. New recipients "authors of matching entries" and "this entry's
  author, once per matching entry" go with it, along with an optional record of
  announced pairs so nobody is introduced twice, shareable between rules.
- Rules: the **Notify matching ride offers and requests** rule type is gone; it is
  an ordinary event notification now. Existing rules are migrated automatically
  into a pair of event-notification rules that share one record of announced pairs
  (one per side of the ride-type field), and the pairs already announced are carried
  over. The upgrade also finishes the removal - its table, message provider, version
  record and queued ad-hoc tasks - so no manual uninstall is needed and cron is not
  left suspended on a missing plugin.
- Email views: added the `##notificationotherentryurl##` and
  `##notificationotherentrylink##` patterns. When a notification is about a pair of
  entries they point at the counterpart of the one being rendered, so a message can
  show the ride that was found and still link back to the reader's own entry.
- Filters: fixed four defects in the "NOT" search path that also affected ordinary
  filters — an OR criterion matching nothing broke the query, a negated duration
  returned exactly the entries it was meant to exclude, a negated time excluded the
  entries that hold no time at all and negated a range only in part, and a negated
  multi-select dropped the entries with no value for the field.

2026-06-29
----------

- Views: added a per-view **permitted filters** whitelist. A view keeps its
  configured filter (now labelled **Default filter**) and can list additional
  filters users may switch to; any other filter is rejected and the default is
  applied. The legacy "filter override" option is now **Allow all filters** and
  supersedes the whitelist. Existing views are migrated so their behavior is
  unchanged. Backup/restore and older backups are supported.
- Rules: added the **Update field** rule type, which writes a fixed value into a
  text, select, radio button, checkbox or multi-select field when triggered
  (with optional follow-up events).
- Rules: event-notification and update-field rules support multi-row **trigger
  conditions** combined with AND/OR and optional NOT.
- Entries: added **timesubmitted** ("Time of final submission"), shown via the
  `[[timesubmitted]]` tag with the `entrytime` field format; set when an entry
  reaches Final submission and cleared if it is moved back.
- Field formats: radio button fields gained a **Stepper progress** display format
  (with optional FontAwesome step icons).
- Fields: the **Text** field type gained a responsive **Input field width**
  setting (value + px/%/em unit).
- Field layouts: the layout editor gained curated Bootstrap-5 **presets**; field
  layouts were renamed from "renderers". Fieldgroup subfields can carry their own
  layout/behavior, and a `:totals` field format adds a numeric totals row.
- Permissions: added capability `mod/datalynx:editfinalsubmission` to allow
  editing entries after they reach Final submission status.
- Documentation: updated the user guides (Views, Rules, Fields, Field Formats,
  Permissions, Patterns & Styling) to cover the above.

2026-04-20
----------

- Updated the bundled PDF.js third-party library to 5.6.205.
- Added `thirdpartylibs.xml` and `pdfjs/readme_moodle.txt` to document the
  vendored PDF.js library and its upgrade process.
